{% extends 'layout.twig' %}

{% macro status(kind) %}
  {%- if kind == 'shipped' -%}<span class="rm-status rm-status-shipped"><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span> Shipped</span>
  {%- elseif kind == 'progress' -%}<span class="rm-status rm-status-progress"><span aria-hidden="true">◐</span> In progress</span>
  {%- elseif kind == 'later' -%}<span class="rm-status rm-status-later"><span aria-hidden="true">○</span> Later</span>
  {%- else -%}<span class="rm-status rm-status-planned"><span aria-hidden="true">○</span> Planned</span>
  {%- endif -%}
{% endmacro %}

{% block body %}
{% import _self as rm %}
  <div class="card roadmap-page">
    <h2>Roadmap</h2>
    <p class="lede">What’s live, what’s coming next and what’s on the to-do list. If something about OSM bugs you, or something is missing, let me know and I’ll see if it’s possible.</p>
    <p class="muted">This page is also the changelog: what went live and when is listed under <a href="#history">Changelog</a>, newest first.</p>

    <div class="rm-legend" aria-label="Status key">
      <span class="rm-legend-title">Key:</span>
      <span class="rm-key">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <span class="rm-legend-text">live now, with the date it went live</span></span>
      <span class="rm-key">{{ rm.status('progress') }} <span class="rm-legend-text">being built</span></span>
      <span class="rm-key">{{ rm.status('planned') }} <span class="rm-legend-text">planned, no date yet</span></span>
      <span class="rm-key">{{ rm.status('later') }} <span class="rm-legend-text">backlog</span></span>
    </div>

    <p class="rm-jump muted">Jump to: <a href="#shipped">Shipped</a> · <a href="#history">Changelog</a> · <a href="#in-progress">In progress</a> · <a href="#planned">Planned</a> · <a href="#later">Later</a></p>

    <section class="help-section" id="shipped" aria-labelledby="shipped-h">
      <h3 id="shipped-h">Shipped</h3>
      <p class="muted">Newest first. The <a href="#history">Changelog</a> below has the details.</p>
      <ul class="rm-list">
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-10-24">24 Oct 2026</time> <span class="rm-area">Sign-in</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Signing in on phones</h4>
          <p>If signing in doesn’t finish, OSMHelper no longer sends you straight back to OSM again and again. It shows a <strong>Continue to OSM</strong> button instead, plain pages that say what probably went wrong and a tip for phones where the OSM app takes over the sign-in. <a href="/help/#signing-in">More in Help</a>.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-10-24">24 Oct 2026</time> <span class="rm-area">Menu</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Tidier menu</h4>
          <p>The menu is now grouped as <strong>People</strong>, <strong>Joining</strong>, <strong>Badges</strong>, <strong>Equipment</strong> and <strong>Finance</strong>. Roadmap is linked at the bottom of every page and from Help. Addresses haven’t changed, so bookmarks still work.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-10-24">24 Oct 2026</time> <span class="rm-area">People</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Young Leaders</h4>
          <p>See which other sections each Young Leader helps in, with a <strong>Helping in</strong> filter, search, sorting and export. Leaders are left out. Loading is paced and stops straight away if your allowance runs low or OSM says too many requests. <a href="/help/#young-leaders">More in Help</a>.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-10-24">24 Oct 2026</time> <span class="rm-area">OSM allowance</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Protect your OSM allowance</h4>
          <p>The waiting list uses fewer OSM requests and is kept for 5 minutes. When your allowance runs low, or OSM asks OSMHelper to slow down, it pauses and says how long to wait instead of risking a lockout. <a href="/help/#osm-busy">More in Help</a>.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-10-22">22 Oct 2026</time> <span class="rm-area">Members</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Events list</h4>
          <p>List a section’s events by start date for a date range or all time, with archived events included and marked Archived. Sort, search, print or download as CSV. Changing the dates or downloading doesn’t use your OSM allowance.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-10-15">15 Oct 2026</time> <span class="rm-area">Members</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Find a member</h4>
          <p>Search by postcode, phone number or parent/contact name across the sections you load. Results show the member, their section and which contact matched. Searching doesn’t use your OSM allowance.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-10-12">12 Oct 2026</time> <span class="rm-area">Equipment</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Add an equipment item</h4>
          <p>Create a quartermaster item from the Equipment page. You review the fields, then OSMHelper saves one new row. Editing an existing item is still planned.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-10-12">12 Oct 2026</time> <span class="rm-area">Group numbers</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Choose sections before loading group numbers</h4>
          <p>Group numbers lists the sections from your OSM sign-in. Tick the ones you need, then load. OSMHelper only fetches those sections, plus the waiting list for the age bands. Explorers, Adults and sections switched off in Settings are left out.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-10-12">12 Oct 2026</time> <span class="rm-area">Members</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Choose sections before loading members</h4>
          <p>The member list shows the sections from your OSM sign-in. Tick the ones you need, then load. OSMHelper only fetches those sections. Member checks still reads every section.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-10-05">5 Oct 2026</time> <span class="rm-area">Waiting list</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">WordPress joining form</h4>
          <p>A waiting-list form for your group’s WordPress website. Parents fill it in and OSMHelper adds the child to your OSM waiting list with your OSM login, so there’s no OSM app to set up for each group. Includes a parent note, confirmation email, address lookup, text-message consent and optional captcha. Set it up under Joining → Joining form.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-09-26">26 Sep 2026</time> <span class="rm-area">Waiting list</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Waiting list rank, dated notes and willing to help</h4>
          <p>Rank applicants, add dated notes and mark who is willing to help, then review and save to your own OSM custom fields. Works with more than one waiting list. The score is explained on the page and stays in OSMHelper.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-09-26">26 Sep 2026</time> <span class="rm-area">Site</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Changelog</h4>
          <p>A dated list of what’s new. Since 28 Sep 2026 it’s part of this page, under <a href="#history">Changelog</a>.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-09-21">21 Sep 2026</time> <span class="rm-area">Badges</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Nights Away tracker</h4>
          <p>Pick one or more members with search (Leaders and Young Leaders are left out) to see nights away per camp from OSM, including named Discovery camps. Sort across members, filter by year and export to PDF with the scout’s name and totals.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-09-06">6 Sep 2026</time> <span class="rm-area">Badges</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Top awards</h4>
          <p>Pick a section to see how close each member is to their top award (Chief Scout’s award), review the suggested progress, then confirm to write it to OSM. Updated on 7 and 8 Sep 2026 with Bronze and Silver awards and rate-limit warnings.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-09-06">6 Sep 2026</time> <span class="rm-area">Finance</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Bank accounts, transactions and All transfers</h4>
          <p>Read your OSM bank accounts and transactions, and see transfers across all accounts with unmatched in/out legs flagged.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-09-06">6 Sep 2026</time> <span class="rm-area">Equipment</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Equipment list, bulk move and locations</h4>
          <p>All your OSM equipment columns in one searchable table, broken items highlighted and bulk moves to locations you set up in Settings.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-09-06">6 Sep 2026</time> <span class="rm-area">Members</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Members, member checks and group numbers</h4>
          <p>Youth members and young leaders in the sections you choose, checks for young people in more than one section, the waiting list and group numbers for the sections you choose, with bar charts.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-09-06">6 Sep 2026</time> <span class="rm-area">Site</span></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Menus, tables, Help and Roadmap</h4>
          <p>Grouped menus with icons, tables you can sort, search and export, the OSM rate limit shown on screen and the Help and Roadmap pages.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section" id="history" aria-labelledby="history-h">
      <h3 id="history-h">Changelog</h3>
      <p class="muted">What changed, newest first. Each entry went live on the date shown.</p>
      <ul class="rm-list">
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped rm-history" id="2026-10-24-signin">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-10-24">24 Oct 2026</time></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Signing in on phones</h4>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>No more sign-in loop:</strong> if you come back to sign in twice within a few minutes without it finishing, OSMHelper shows a <strong>Continue to OSM</strong> button instead of sending you straight back to OSM. The same happens if you sign in several times in a few minutes but this browser doesn’t keep you signed in, with a reminder to check that cookies are allowed.</li>
            <li><strong>Plainer retry pages:</strong> if sign-in seems to have started in a different browser or app, or OSM cancelled or refused it, a short page says what usually causes it and has a <strong>Try again here</strong> button.</li>
            <li><strong>Phone tip:</strong> these pages explain how to stop the OSM app opening the sign-in link on Android, or in Firefox. Chrome has no setting for this.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped rm-history" id="2026-10-24-menu">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-10-24">24 Oct 2026</time></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Tidier menu</h4>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>People:</strong> Group numbers, Member list, Find a member, Young Leaders and Member checks.</li>
            <li><strong>Joining:</strong> Waiting list and Joining form.</li>
            <li><strong>Badges:</strong> Events, Nights away and Top awards.</li>
            <li><strong>Equipment:</strong> the Equipment list, with shortcuts to Add an item and Locations.</li>
            <li><strong>Finance:</strong> Bank accounts and All transfers.</li>
            <li>Roadmap has moved to the bottom of every page and the top of Help. The page you’re on is highlighted in the menu. On phones the menu works without JavaScript, and an open menu fits on a small screen. Addresses haven’t changed, so bookmarks still work.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped rm-history" id="2026-10-24-young-leaders">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-10-24">24 Oct 2026</time></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Young Leaders</h4>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>People → Young Leaders:</strong> choose a section to see which other sections each member helps in, with a <strong>Helping in</strong> filter, search, sorting and CSV, Excel or PDF export. Leaders in the Leaders patrol are left out.</li>
            <li><strong>Paced loading:</strong> one OSM request for the member list, then one per member, with at least a second between requests and a progress bar. Sections of more than 40 ask you to confirm first and sections of more than 150 aren’t loaded. Loading stops straight away if your allowance runs low, OSM says too many requests or anything goes wrong.</li>
            <li><strong>Kept briefly:</strong> only names, ages and section names are kept for up to 2 hours and deleted when you sign out. Going back to the page or filtering doesn’t use your allowance. <strong>Refresh from OSM</strong> can be used once every 5 minutes per section.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped rm-history" id="2026-10-24-osm-allowance">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-10-24">24 Oct 2026</time></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Protect your OSM allowance</h4>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Waiting list:</strong> reads the list and everyone’s waiting list fields in two requests, plus one per applicant for their dates (up to 40 per page load), instead of two per applicant. The result is kept for 5 minutes, so switching between the list and ranking pages doesn’t use more of your allowance.</li>
            <li><strong>Pausing:</strong> when your allowance runs low OSMHelper pauses page loads for your login until it resets. If OSM says too many requests it stops everything for your login, shows “OSM is busy, try again in N minutes” and never retries on its own.</li>
            <li>See <a href="/help/#osm-busy">Help → “OSM is busy”</a> for the details.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped rm-history" id="2026-10-22-privacy">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-10-22">22 Oct 2026</time></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Privacy tightening</h4>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Sessions end after 2 hours:</strong> every session ends 2 hours after you sign in, even while you’re using it, or when you sign out, and its file on the server is cleaned up shortly after. Each page shows when your session ends, and after signing in again you go back to the page you were on. Everyone is signed out once when this goes live.</li>
            <li><strong>Find a member and Nights away:</strong> searches, and the members you pick in Nights away, are sent privately, so postcodes, phone numbers, names and member numbers no longer appear in web addresses, browser history or server logs.</li>
            <li><strong>WordPress joining form:</strong> the OSM access key kept for the form is now encrypted on the server, including keys saved before this change.</li>
            <li><strong>Error logs:</strong> only what failed, the error code and which section; never OSM’s message text, names, contact details or member numbers (older entries were cleaned the same way). Entries are deleted after 30 days.</li>
            <li><strong>What’s saved:</strong> your group settings, with your OSM user number so we know whose settings are whose.</li>
            <li>Leftover debug files that could hold member data have been removed from the code entirely. See <a href="/help/#privacy">Help → Your data and privacy</a>.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped rm-history" id="2026-10-22-events">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-10-22">22 Oct 2026</time></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Events list</h4>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Badges → Events:</strong> choose a section to see its events by start date, oldest first, for a date range (dd/mm/yyyy) or all time. Archived events are included and marked Archived.</li>
            <li><strong>Download CSV:</strong> Section, Start date, Event name and Archived (Yes/No) for the dates you chose, made from the loaded list.</li>
            <li>Load events uses 2 OSM requests per section, never one per event, at most once every 5 minutes per section, stopping straight away on any error or if your allowance runs low. Changing the dates, sorting and the CSV don’t call OSM.</li>
            <li>The list is held in your session for up to about 2 hours, and cleared when it expires or when you sign out.</li>
            <li>Events needs OSM’s “read events” permission. If you signed in before 22 Oct 2026, sign out, sign in again and allow Events when OSM asks.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped rm-history" id="2026-10-15-find-member">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-10-15">15 Oct 2026</time></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Find a member</h4>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>People → Find a member:</strong> find who a postcode, phone number or parent/contact name belongs to. Searches the member’s own details, Primary contacts 1 and 2 and the Emergency contact. Part of a value is enough; phone numbers match with or without +44 and spaces.</li>
            <li>Tick sections and choose Load contacts: one OSM request per section, at most once every 5 minutes, stopping straight away on any error or if your allowance runs low. Searching never calls OSM.</li>
            <li>The contact details are held temporarily in your session on our server for up to about 2 hours, and cleared when they expire or when you sign out.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped rm-history" id="2026-10-12-equipment-add">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-10-12">12 Oct 2026</time></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Add an equipment item</h4>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Equipment:</strong> add a row to one of your quartermaster lists. Name is required. Quantity, description, condition, broken, location, purchase date, notes and renewal price match the OSM columns.</li>
            <li>You review the fields, then Confirm creates one row. Cancel writes nothing. Editing an existing item is still planned.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped rm-history" id="2026-10-12-numbers">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-10-12">12 Oct 2026</time></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Choose sections before loading group numbers</h4>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Group numbers:</strong> the page lists the sections from your OSM sign-in. Tick the ones you need, then load. OSMHelper only fetches those sections.</li>
            <li>The waiting list is still read on that load, so the age bands can be filled in. Explorers, Adults and sections switched off in Settings are not offered.</li>
            <li>The charts and tables stay until you load a different set or sign out. Sign in again if a section is missing.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped rm-history" id="2026-10-12">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-10-12">12 Oct 2026</time></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Choose sections before loading members</h4>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Members:</strong> the page lists the sections from your OSM sign-in. Tick the ones you need, then load. OSMHelper only fetches those sections.</li>
            <li>The list stays until you load a different set or sign out. Sign in again if a section is missing.</li>
            <li><strong>Member checks</strong> still reads every section on this login, so a young person in two sections still shows up.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped rm-history" id="2026-10-05">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-10-05">5 Oct 2026</time></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">WordPress joining form</h4>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Waiting-list form for your website:</strong> a WordPress plugin adds a form with the <code>[osm_waiting_list]</code> shortcode. When a parent sends it, OSMHelper adds the child to your OSM waiting list using your OSM login. Parents don’t need an OSM login, and groups don’t need their own OSM app or API keys.</li>
            <li><strong>What’s saved in OSM:</strong> the child’s name, date of birth and home address (line 1, line 2, town, county, postcode) and up to two parents as Primary Contacts 1 and 2.</li>
            <li><strong>Text messages:</strong> each parent can tick “Receive text messages from Leaders?”, which turns on OSM’s receive-texts setting for their phone.</li>
            <li><strong>Parent note:</strong> an optional note is added to the waiting list’s Notes field (the one chosen in Rank &amp; notes) as a dated line marked “Parent (website form)”. If no Notes field is chosen, the child is still added.</li>
            <li><strong>In WordPress:</strong> a confirmation email to parents with your own reply-to address, Google reCAPTCHA or Cloudflare Turnstile against spam and address lookup with Google address search or a free postcodes.io postcode check.</li>
            <li><strong>Joining form page:</strong> a new <a href="/wordpress-form/">Joining → Joining form</a> page has the plugin download, your site key and waiting-list choice (moved from Settings), step-by-step setup and troubleshooting.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped rm-history" id="2026-09-28">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-09-28">28 Sep 2026</time></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Clearer homepage, one Roadmap and changelog page</h4>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>New homepage:</strong> a plainer, first-person homepage with real screenshots of the tools (all using made-up names), a short note on why OSMHelper exists and a clear “Before you connect” section.</li>
            <li><strong>One page for plans and changes:</strong> the Changelog is now part of this Roadmap page. Old <code>/changelog/</code> links bring you here.</li>
            <li><strong>Menu on phones:</strong> when you’re not signed in, the Menu button now shows on small screens, so Home, Help and Roadmap can be reached.</li>
            <li><strong>Footer and contact:</strong> the footer now says who runs OSMHelper and that it isn’t made or endorsed by Online Scout Manager or The Scout Association. It also gives an email address for questions.</li>
            <li><strong>Less kept on the server:</strong> Top awards results are deleted from the server after 2 hours and when you log out, debug files are off and the error log strips names and contact details.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped rm-history" id="2026-09-27">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-09-27">27 Sep 2026</time></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Clearer roadmap</h4>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Status at a glance:</strong> the <a href="/roadmap/">Roadmap</a> now groups items as Shipped, In progress, Planned and Later. Each item has a labelled badge with a symbol, not just a colour, and there’s a key at the top.</li>
            <li><strong>Dates:</strong> shipped items show the date they went live, newest first. The Nights Away tracker, Top awards, Finance, Equipment and Members tools are now listed as shipped.</li>
            </ul>
        </li>
        <li class="rm-item rm-shipped rm-history" id="2026-09-26">
          <div class="rm-head">{{ rm.status('shipped') }} <time datetime="2026-09-26">26 Sep 2026</time></div>
          <h4 class="rm-title">Waiting list ranking</h4>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Rank &amp; notes:</strong> leaders can give each applicant a rank (1 = first to be offered a place) and add notes, then review exactly what will change before saving to OSM. Values live in your own OSM custom fields; OSMHelper only remembers which fields to use, shared across your group.</li>
            <li><strong>Dated notes:</strong> a new note is added at the top of the existing notes as <code>dd/mm/yy hh:mm - your name - "note"</code> (UK time), so earlier notes are kept.</li>
            <li><strong>Willing to help:</strong> optionally choose an OSM field for it on the Fields page. It can be set to Yes, No or blank from the ranking page and adds 20 to the score when it’s yes.</li>
            <li><strong>More than one waiting list:</strong> pick a list at the top of each page; each list is set up separately.</li>
            <li><strong>Score explained:</strong> the Waiting list and ranking pages now say how the score works, and hovering over or tapping a score shows the breakdown. The score stays in OSMHelper and is never saved to OSM.</li>
            <li><strong>Safer saving:</strong> changes are re-read from OSM before saving, saved one at a time (stopping at the first problem), then checked in OSM; the results page shows what was sent and what OSM now holds.</li>
            <li><strong>Exports:</strong> CSV, Excel and PDF from the Waiting list and ranking pages include every row (even when searching) and the values you’ve typed.</li>
            <li><strong>Menus:</strong> the Members, Badges and Finance menus now close when you click elsewhere, press Escape or choose an item.</li>
            </ul>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section" id="in-progress" aria-labelledby="in-progress-h">
      <h3 id="in-progress-h">In progress</h3>
